[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2364819922","pull_request_review_id":3247553290,"id":2364819922,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6M9EnS","diff_hunk":"@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@ class Dictionary {\n \n \tint size() const;\n \tbool is_empty() const;\n+\tvoid reserve(uint32_t p_new_capacity);","path":"core/variant/dictionary.h","commit_id":"0628323069457aba5dab9a951699cb63ff77e8af","original_commit_id":"a60202688a5c1b9c003426d2d99cd868ac5f6c6f","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"While `uint32_t` would be appropriate for internal use, I think for `Dictionary` it should use `int64_t` input. The reason being that it's generally outwards facing (even if `reserve` isn't exposed yet), and therefore it needs defensive interfaces.\r\n\r\nThe function should then check for negative values and values larger than `uint32_t` before casting down.\r\n\r\nI realize that other APIs currently use `int` instead. That's also not appropriate imo, and should be changed in some future PR.","created_at":"2025-09-19T23:31:25Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T23:41:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#discussion_r2364819922","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110709","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2364819922"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#discussion_r2364819922"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110709"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2364819922/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2365252309","pull_request_review_id":3248244179,"id":2365252309,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6M-uLV","diff_hunk":"@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@ class Dictionary {\n \n \tint size() const;\n \tbool is_empty() const;\n+\tvoid reserve(uint32_t p_new_capacity);","path":"core/variant/dictionary.h","commit_id":"0628323069457aba5dab9a951699cb63ff77e8af","original_commit_id":"a60202688a5c1b9c003426d2d99cd868ac5f6c6f","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I've been doing some comparisons to #105928 (adds `reserve()` to `CowData`, consequently to `Vector`, `Array` and `String`). I noticed that `CowData`'s `reserve()` there uses an `uint64_t`, while `Vector`'s uses `int64_t`.\r\n\r\nComparing to this one, `HashMap` uses `uint32_t`. Would using an `int64_t` input here really be wise?","created_at":"2025-09-20T04:08:00Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T04:08:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#discussion_r2365252309","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110709","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2365252309"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#discussion_r2365252309"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110709"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2365252309/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2364819922,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2365262158","pull_request_review_id":3248258406,"id":2365262158,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6M-wlO","diff_hunk":"@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@ class Dictionary {\n \n \tint size() const;\n \tbool is_empty() const;\n+\tvoid reserve(uint32_t p_new_capacity);","path":"core/variant/dictionary.h","commit_id":"0628323069457aba5dab9a951699cb63ff77e8af","original_commit_id":"a60202688a5c1b9c003426d2d99cd868ac5f6c6f","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"My sentiment on unsigned integers is \"avoid at all costs\", unless you have an explicit and very strong reason to use an unsigned integer.\r\n\r\nThis should use `int64_t`, especially if you expect it to be exposed to GDS, where `int` is always `int64_t`.\r\n\r\nIt should be coupled with size checks that the expected size is `> 0 ` and `< uint32_t max` to bind to the `HashMap` API.","created_at":"2025-09-20T04:14:17Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T04:14:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#discussion_r2365262158","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110709","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2365262158"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#discussion_r2365262158"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110709"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2365262158/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2364819922,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2365554909","pull_request_review_id":3248962409,"id":2365554909,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6M_4Dd","diff_hunk":"@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@ class Dictionary {\n \n \tint size() const;\n \tbool is_empty() const;\n+\tvoid reserve(uint32_t p_new_capacity);","path":"core/variant/dictionary.h","commit_id":"0628323069457aba5dab9a951699cb63ff77e8af","original_commit_id":"a60202688a5c1b9c003426d2d99cd868ac5f6c6f","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@DeeJayLSP https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105928 is a fair comparison (we ended with `int` there). \r\nI think the main difference there is what ATS was concerned about: With the `int64_t` API, `reserve` would have been able to reserve more elements than would be fillable / indexable with the current API. This is not the case here, where the full `uint32_t` spectrum is usable.\r\n\r\nIn general, I differentiate two different API types: Those that are user facing, and those that are internal for high performance.\r\nThe internal APIs should use the fastest / smallest type (e.g. an unsigned int for `reserve`, because negative values are not supported). It is expected that the caller knows what they're doing, and passes valid values.\r\nUser facing APIs on the other hand should use whatever type the user is most likely to have (which is `int64_t`). We should then make the necessary defensive checks before passing the value to the high performance API.\r\n\r\nFor this reason (and the current `size` limitation), I plan to change the `Array` API to use `int64_t` in a future PR.","created_at":"2025-09-20T09:25:38Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T09:30:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#discussion_r2365554909","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110709","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2365554909"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#discussion_r2365554909"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110709"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2365554909/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":77,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2364819922,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2365555554","pull_request_review_id":3248963042,"id":2365555554,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOA